    "body": "`parse_dependencies()` did not record `pkg.submodule` for `from pkg cimport submodule`, so `cythonize` did not notice changes to `pkg/submodule.pxd` and reused stale generated code.\n\n`dependency_after_from_regex` was anchored with `^` and applied with `search(source, pos=m.end())`. Since that position is on the same line as `cimport`, a name there never matched and the search skipped to the next indented line. For example, `from pkg cimport sub` followed by an indented `pass` recorded `pkg.pass`, and a parenthesised multi-line import only recorded its first line. This broke in 2018 when the source slice became `pos=` and `re.M` was added.\n\nI now use `match()` at that position, allow newlines inside the parentheses, and skip empty items and `as` aliases. The new tests in `TestDependencies.py` fail on master and pass with this change.\n\nFixes #8091\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-31T18:06:50Z",
